    "result_text": "Build succeeds and both tests pass (the full test suite here is the acceptance tests).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `locality` derivation from an owner's city, following the existing pattern for derived read-only fields (`initials`, `membershipTier`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/CityRegionTable.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility class holding the fixed city\u2192region table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) with one `regionFor(city)` lookup that returns the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"`. This is the single source of truth for the mapping.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getLocality()` getter that delegates to `CityRegionTable.regionFor(city)`. It sits alongside the other pure derived getters and keeps the entity thin (no table data embedded in it).\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared `locality` as a `readOnly` string property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field and MapStruct maps it by name automatically (same mechanism as `membershipTier`/`initials`).\n\nThe `locality` value flows out unchanged on `GET /api/owners/{id}`: `NSW` for Sydney, `UNKNOWN` for an unlisted city \u2014 matching both acceptance tests.",
